WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.989 --> 00:00:06.350
In A Song of Ice and Fire and Game of Thrones,
dragonglass, or obsidian, is a mysterious

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:11.340
material with special magical properties relating
to white walkers and dragons.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:15.719
It’s used by the children of the forest
and the Night’s Watch, and may play an important

00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:17.840
role in the ending of the series.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.439
So let’s have a look.

00:00:19.439 --> 00:00:23.890
Obsidian exists in the real world – it’s
a volcanic glass that forms from cooled lava.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:28.279
Historically, obsidian’s been highly valued,
because as well as being quite beautiful,

00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:31.449
it can be fractured to form really sharp edges.

00:00:31.449 --> 00:00:35.520
So for thousands of years, all over the world
, it’s been used to make tools and weapons

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.630
like blades and arrowheads, as well as objects
of artistic and religious significance.

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:46.460
On Easter Island, the Moai statues had obsidian
for eyes, in Anatolia, mirrors were made out

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:52.160
of obsidian, and in Mesoamerica, the Aztecs
used obsidian knives in bloodletting rituals

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:53.960
and human sacrifice.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:59.490
Now, obsidian is used to make surgical scalpels
with blades sharper than steel, is considered

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:05.260
a magical stone by various New-Agey folks,
and is a high-tier crafting material in Minecraft

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:10.270
and Terraria, so in a way, we still seem to
value obsidian to this day.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:14.539
Anyway, in Game of Thrones, obsidian has basically
the same physical properties that it has in

00:01:14.539 --> 00:01:15.539
the real world.

00:01:15.539 --> 00:01:20.200
It’s apparently formed from volcanic activity
though there are alternative theories . It’s

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:25.549
“slick and shiny” and usually black, though
can be other colours . It’s very “brittle”,

00:01:25.549 --> 00:01:27.859
and can form “razor sharp” edges.

00:01:27.859 --> 00:01:32.829
And it’s been used by ancient peoples for
thousands of years, though in Game of Thrones,

00:01:32.829 --> 00:01:35.579
those people aren’t humans.

00:01:35.579 --> 00:01:39.960
The original inhabitants of Westeros are the
giants, and the children of the forest . The

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.249
giants apparently “knew of no better tools
or weapons than branches pulled from trees”

00:01:44.249 --> 00:01:48.369
, but the children of the forest “had great
art in working obsidian”, and used it “to

00:01:48.369 --> 00:01:53.920
make tools and weapons for hunting” . Eventually,
human settlers came to Westeros – the First

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:58.799
Men, and later the Andals, who all but wiped
out the giants and children, who now only

00:01:58.799 --> 00:02:04.649
survive in small numbers north of the Wall
. But the humans value obsidian too – it’s

00:02:04.649 --> 00:02:09.720
traded , and used in ornamentation – in
sword hilts, and rings and things – Crowfood

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:14.980
Umber wears a chunk of dragonglass in his
empty eye socket . So obsidian is, around,

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:18.840
in small amounts, but it’s only during the
events of A Song of Ice and Fire that people

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.630
start to realise just how important obsidian
is.

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:28.060
In Clash, Jon Snow finds a cache of obsidian
weapons, wrapped up in a Night’s Watch cloak

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:32.390
and buried on the Fist of the First Men . The
cloak hasn’t rotted, suggesting that the

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:37.330
obsidian was recently buried , so it might
have been Benjen Stark who left it , or maybe

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:39.320
Coldhands for Bloodraven.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:43.730
In the show it’s a bit different – Grenn
and Sam find the cache beneath a stone marked

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:48.020
with runes of the First Men, suggesting that
it might have been left by ancient Night’s

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:51.760
Watchmen . Whoever buried it, Jon takes some
of the obsidian, and gives it to his friends

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:56.970
in the Watch . Sam gets one of the daggers
, and discovers its importance when the Others

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:57.970
come.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:02.930
The Others, or white walkers, are “strange”
icy creatures from beyond the Wall who’ve

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:09.040
been killing humans and raising them as wights,
basically zombies, in an army of the dead,

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:14.280
apparently intent on killing everything that
lives . It may actually be more complicated

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:18.340
than that, but either way, it is looking like
the Night’s Watch will have to stop them.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:22.600
The wights can be killed with fire , or by
chopping them into bits , but the Others are

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:26.991
really hard to kill – they’re apparently
invulnerable to most normal blades , and we’ve

00:03:26.991 --> 00:03:28.850
never seen them hurt by fire.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:33.150
The only thing that we’ve seen kill a white
walker, at least in the books, is Sam’s

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:38.250
obsidian dagger . When Sam stabs a walker
with obsidian, the walker dissolves, melts

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:43.420
away, its body smoking and steaming where
it touches the dagger – this stuff is, like,

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:48.540
white walker kryptonite, it has a fiery magic
to it which is hugely destructive to the icy

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:53.470
white walkers . So the Night’s Watch wants
more obsidian . All they have now are the

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:57.100
few daggers and arrowheads and stuff that
Jon took from the First of the First Men , and

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:01.020
also some wildlings have obsidian weapons
. There’s still lots more obsidian at the

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:05.340
Fist – or at Hardhome, in the show – but
with all these wights and walkers around,

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:08.280
it’d be too dangerous to go back for the
cache.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:13.350
So as Jeor Mormont says, they “need to find
dragonglass someplace else” . Luckily for

00:04:13.350 --> 00:04:17.250
the Watch, there are at least four different
places they could get some.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:21.009
Firstly, when Stannis Baratheon comes to the
Wall, he agrees with the Watch that they need

00:04:21.009 --> 00:04:23.169
to get more obsidian to fight the Others.

00:04:23.169 --> 00:04:27.629
He says that on the island of Dragonstone,
where he originally ruled, there are tunnels

00:04:27.629 --> 00:04:31.910
full of obsidian, whole “Chunks of it, boulders
[and] ledges”.

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:37.030
So Stannis orders his men back on Dragonstone
to start mining this obsidian . The only problem

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:41.449
is that, in the next book, Dragonstone is
besieged and captured by the forces of King

00:04:41.449 --> 00:04:46.129
Tommen , and we don’t know whether any of
Stannis’ obsidian makes it off the island.

00:04:46.129 --> 00:04:51.030
Mace Tyrell says that after its capture, “No
wealth [is] found on Dragonstone”, that

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:55.129
“every inch” of the island is searched,
and not “a single gemstone or speck of gold”

00:04:55.129 --> 00:05:01.190
[is] found , though Kevan Lannister doubts
this . So basically it’s uncertain, but

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:05.290
possible, that some of the obsidian mined
on Dragonstone makes it off the island and

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:09.889
is shipped towards the Wall – maybe to arrive
in the next book.

00:05:09.889 --> 00:05:12.969
The second way the Watch could get obsidian
is from Skagos.

00:05:12.969 --> 00:05:18.129
Skagos is a big island just east of the Wall,
and its people, the Skagosi, are infamous

00:05:18.129 --> 00:05:24.590
for savagery, cannibalism , human sacrifice,
and, apparently, riding unicorns . In Dance,

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:29.340
Davos sets sail for Skagos because apparently
Rickon Stark is taken there by Osha . So it

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:33.939
looks like Skagos will be an important location
in the next book, and the thing is, the Skagosi

00:05:33.939 --> 00:05:40.389
are known to offer obsidian blades in trade
– Skagos may be a source of obsidian for

00:05:40.389 --> 00:05:41.729
the Watch.

00:05:41.729 --> 00:05:45.830
So with any luck, we’ll soon see Rickon
Stark riding a unicorn to the Wall, with a

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:49.349
big stash of dragonglass to fight the Others.

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:51.371
The third possible source of obsidian is Valyria.

00:05:51.371 --> 00:05:56.020
Valyria is where the Targaryens and their
dragons originally came from – it was once

00:05:56.020 --> 00:06:01.310
the centre of a huge, powerful empire , but
was destroyed in a massive, mysterious, fiery

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:04.280
apocalypse known as the Doom of Valyria.

00:06:04.280 --> 00:06:07.970
We don’t really know what caused the Doom,
but it seems to have been volcanic , and part

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:13.719
of the destruction involved dragonglass raining
down from the sky – so presumably there’s

00:06:13.719 --> 00:06:16.740
a whole lot of obsidian still lying around
in the ruins of Valyria.

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:22.020
Valyria is now considered a cursed , dangerous
place, avoided by just about everyone , but

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:27.000
if, say, Daenerys Targaryen was brave enough
to stop off at her ancestral homeland on her

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:31.229
way to Westeros, she might just be able to
pick up a supply of obsidian.

00:06:31.229 --> 00:06:35.430
Imagine her turning up at the Wall when the
walkers come knocking, bringing not only fire-breathing

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:40.509
dragons but enough obsidian to arm every man
on the Wall – that would be a perfect way

00:06:40.509 --> 00:06:44.500
to stop the Others – and for Daenerys to
prove herself to the realm she intends to

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:45.509
rule.

00:06:45.509 --> 00:06:49.039
This is just speculation, and George Martin
has been kind of ambivalent about whether

00:06:49.039 --> 00:06:53.879
we’ll actually see Valyria – though it
has been shown in the show – so, we don’t

00:06:53.879 --> 00:06:54.879
know.

00:06:54.879 --> 00:06:58.810
It seems – maybe not likely, but surely
possible – that Dany will deliver obsidian

00:06:58.810 --> 00:07:00.909
from Valyria.

00:07:00.909 --> 00:07:04.669
The fourth possible source of obsidian is
the children of the forest . We know that

00:07:04.669 --> 00:07:07.889
they’ve used obsidian for thousands of years,
we know that the children still exist north

00:07:07.889 --> 00:07:12.210
of the Wall, and we are told that last time
the Others came, thousands of years ago, they

00:07:12.210 --> 00:07:16.050
were stopped with the help of the children
of the forest , which seems to have involved

00:07:16.050 --> 00:07:20.340
the children providing the Night’s Watch
with obsidian . This may also be related to

00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:25.349
the legendary hero Azor Ahai, or the “last
hero”, a figure who apparently led humanity

00:07:25.349 --> 00:07:30.669
against the white walkers with a flaming sword
called Lightbringer . Some fans speculate

00:07:30.669 --> 00:07:35.659
that this magic sword may have been made of
obsidian, or some obsidian alloy, because

00:07:35.659 --> 00:07:40.009
many of the powers of Lightbringer can be
explained by the properties of obsidian – it

00:07:40.009 --> 00:07:44.620
kills white walkers, it burns without being
consumed , it can emit bright light . A tale

00:07:44.620 --> 00:07:49.369
of Azor Ahai says when he stabbed a monster
with Lightbringer, the creature steamed and

00:07:49.369 --> 00:07:54.419
smoked and melted – just as a white walker
steams and smokes and melts when Sam stabs

00:07:54.419 --> 00:07:58.810
it with obsidian . So there seems to be a
connection here between Azor Ahai’s magical

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:00.699
sword and obsidian.

00:08:00.699 --> 00:08:05.009
Maybe the children of the forest will help
Azor Ahai forge another Lightbringer – or

00:08:05.009 --> 00:08:09.979
maybe Lightbringer was actually not one sword,
but the many hundreds of obsidian weapons

00:08:09.979 --> 00:08:14.089
given to the Night’s Watch by the children
– which, over thousands of years, became

00:08:14.089 --> 00:08:18.659
the myth of a single hero and his magic sword
saving the world.

00:08:18.659 --> 00:08:20.660
For now, we don’t know.

00:08:20.660 --> 00:08:24.590
The point here is that the children of the
forest may give the Watch obsidian, and this

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:28.599
could also be related to this Azor Ahai prophecy
business somehow.

00:08:28.599 --> 00:08:32.460
That makes four really cool ways that the
Night’s Watch could get obsidian to fight

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:37.130
the Others, and decide the outcome of what
may be the biggest conflict in the conclusion

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:38.130
of the series.

00:08:38.130 --> 00:08:43.210
But there’s still another reason why obsidian
is important – glass candles.

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:48.279
Glass candles are magical artefacts from Valyria,
tall, twisted chunks of obsidian that can

00:08:48.279 --> 00:08:50.259
function as candles.

00:08:50.259 --> 00:08:53.750
They seem to be closely connected to the power
of magic in the world – apparently no one

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:58.790
had succeeded in lighting a glass candle for
many many years , until the recent reawakening

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:04.180
of magic with the birth of new dragons, and
the return of the white walkers . In Feast,

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:08.730
we see that Marwyn the Mage has succeeded
in lighting a glass candle, which symbolises

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:10.449
this magical reawakening.

00:09:10.449 --> 00:09:15.100
But glass candles aren’t just symbolic,
they’re also very powerful tools.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:19.310
Marwyn says that “The sorcerers of [Valyria]
could see across mountains, seas, and deserts

00:09:19.310 --> 00:09:20.700
with … glass candles.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:24.770
They could enter a man’s dreams and give
him visions, and speak to one another half

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:30.140
a world apart” . We’ve actually already
seen this magic at work – Quaithe, the mysterious

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:35.660
Asshai’i shadowbinder, appears to Daenerys
in strange dreams and gives her cryptic advice,

00:09:35.660 --> 00:09:41.959
apparently using a glass candle . This use
of fire magic to see across long distances

00:09:41.959 --> 00:09:46.750
and enter peoples’ dreams contrasts with
the magic of the old gods and the weirwoods,

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:51.400
which Bloodraven and Bran use to do the same
things – to see across long distances , and

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:56.690
enter peoples’ dreams . The way Melisandre
and Moqorro see visions in their flames may

00:09:56.690 --> 00:10:02.630
also be related here, cause it also seems
a similar magic – using fire to see images.

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:06.519
So all this gives a sense of order to the
magic in this world.

00:10:06.519 --> 00:10:10.769
Anyway we know Marwyn and Quaithe have glass
candles, and it’s actually possible that

00:10:10.769 --> 00:10:15.209
using them to communicate and work together
– because when Quaithe warns Daenerys about

00:10:15.209 --> 00:10:18.759
everyone who’s coming for her, she leaves
out Marwyn.

00:10:18.759 --> 00:10:22.740
As well as Quaithe and Marwyn, glass candles
are owned by the other maesters of the Citadel,

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:27.610
someone called Urrathon Night-Walker in Qarth,
and also the Targaryens of Aemon’s day seem

00:10:27.610 --> 00:10:28.610
to have had some.

00:10:28.610 --> 00:10:32.430
We don’t know much about how these candles
are being used, but they’re obviously very

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:35.529
powerful, and could maybe play a big role
in the future of the series.

00:10:35.529 --> 00:10:39.519
Hopefully we’ll learn more about glass candles
while Sam is at the Citadel.

00:10:39.519 --> 00:10:40.649
Anyway.

00:10:40.649 --> 00:10:43.800
That is pretty much everything we know about
obsidian.

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:47.921
It kills white walkers, so the Night’s Watch
will probably need some, and luckily, there

00:10:47.921 --> 00:10:50.639
are a bunch of interesting ways they could
get more.

00:10:50.639 --> 00:10:54.110
There also glass candles, which we don’t
know much about, but could also be really

00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:55.509
important later on.

00:10:55.509 --> 00:10:56.759
Thanks for watching.

00:10:56.759 --> 00:11:00.579
Feel free to like and subscribe if you’d
like to see more, and thanks also to all the

00:11:00.579 --> 00:11:05.740
Patrons who support this channel, including
